  {"claim_ref": "book_0103::lead_book_0103_3_006", "verdict": "corroboration", "behavior_id": "dow_theory_average_confirmation", "page": 1, "exact_text": "Breakouts in the Dow Industrials should, as a rule, be\nconfirmed by similar breakouts in both the S&P 500 and the NYSE\nComposite Index if the breakout is to have staying power.", "added_conditions": [], "added_parameters": []},
  {"claim_ref": "book_0103::lead_book_0103_3_007", "verdict": "corroboration", "behavior_id": "relative_strength_ranking", "page": 1, "exact_text": "When the small stocks\nare showing poor relative strength, or are lagging too far behind\nthe large stocks, that’s often a warning that market breadth is\nweakening.", "added_conditions": [], "added_parameters": []},
  {"claim_ref": "book_0103::lead_book_0103_3_008", "verdict": "corroboration", "behavior_id": "dow_theory_average_confirmation", "page": 1, "exact_text": "A Dow Theory buy sig-\nnal is present when both averages hit new highs. When one\ndiverges from the other, a caution signal is given.", "added_conditions": [], "added_parameters": []},
  {"claim_ref": "book_0103::lead_book_0103_2_006", "verdict": "corroboration", "behavior_id": "trend_following_channel", "page": 1, "exact_text": "Prices crossed the upper channel in early 1995 (see circle) to give a buy signal\nwhich remains in effect 3 years later. A close beneath the lower line is needed\nto give a sell signal.", "added_conditions": [], "added_parameters": [{"name": "channel length", "value": "4 months", "page": 1}]},
  {"claim_ref": "book_0103::lead_book_0103_2_007", "verdict": "generic", "behavior_id": null, "page": null, "exact_text": null, "added_conditions": [], "added_parameters": []},
  {"claim_ref": "book_0103::lead_book_0103_3_012", "verdict": "corroboration", "behavior_id": "relative_strength_ranking", "page": 1, "exact_text": "These traders move funds out of stocks and stock\ngroups that are showing poor momentum and into those that are\nshowing good momentum. They use a technique called relative\nstrength.", "added_conditions": [], "added_parameters": []},
  {"claim_ref": "book_0103::lead_book_0103_2_008", "verdict": "generic", "behavior_id": null, "page": null, "exact_text": null, "added_conditions": [], "added_parameters": []},
  {"claim_ref": "book_0103::lead_book_0103_3_014", "verdict": "corroboration", "behavior_id": "momentum_divergence_reversal", "page": 1, "exact_text": "While prices made lower lows (line A), the DI formed high-\ner lows (line B). This is a classic positive, or bullish divergence,\nwhich suggested that bond prices were bottoming.", "added_conditions": [], "added_parameters": []},
  {"claim_ref": "book_0103::lead_book_0103_2_010", "verdict": "corroboration", "behavior_id": "line_crossover_momentum", "page": 1, "exact_text": "Some traders regard a crossing above the zero line as a\nbuy signal and a crossing below the line as a sell signal", "added_conditions": [], "added_parameters": []},
  {"claim_ref": "book_0103::lead_book_0103_3_017", "verdict": "generic", "behavior_id": null, "page": null, "exact_text": null, "added_conditions": [], "added_parameters": []},
  {"claim_ref": "book_0103::lead_book_0103_2_012", "verdict": "corroboration", "behavior_id": "line_crossover_momentum", "page": 1, "exact_text": "If the\nshorter average crosses below the longer average, however, a trend\nreversal is signaled.", "added_conditions": [], "added_parameters": []},
  {"claim_ref": "book_0103::lead_book_0103_3_022", "verdict": "corroboration", "behavior_id": "mean_reversion_band", "page": 1, "exact_text": "Points 1 and 3 show prices bouncing after dipping below the\nlower band. Point 2 shows prices falling after rising above the upper band.", "added_conditions": [], "added_parameters": [{"name": "Starc band moving average length", "value": "6 weeks", "page": 1}, {"name": "Keltner ATR lookback periods", "value": "10", "page": 1}, {"name": "Keltner EMA lookback periods", "value": "20", "page": 1}, {"name": "Keltner ATR multiplier", "value": "2", "page": 1}]},
